<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - SAMANCOR YEAR SHR DOWN, DIV CUT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SAMANCOR YEAR SHR DOWN, DIV CUT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - before exceps	 127	   vs 302</p>
<p>    - after exceps	  214	   vs 355</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 70	    vs 170</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   409.25	vs 675.92</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   510.15	vs 839.04</p>
<p>    Tax			 46.75	 vs 169.65</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   44.28	 vs 5.86</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,702.49    vs 3,791.76</p>
<p>    Profit on disposals   255.38	vs 122.58</p>
<p>Provision against investments 59.78 loss vs nil</p>
<p>Medical aid restructuring cost nil vs 22.50</p>
<p>Provisions against discont ops 47.25 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net tax credit on exceps 18.76    vs 1.56</p>
<p>Div payable Sept 26</p>
<p>on register Sept 12</p>
<p>Full name: Samancor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts for pre-exceptional earnings per share were on a range of 120 cents to 172 and the dividend was seen being slashed from 170 cents to a range of 50 cents to 80.</p>
<p>The consensus figures were for earnings of 142 cents a share and a shareholder payout of 67 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
